        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this fabulous two-bedroom, two-bathroom apartment to the market within the quiet and highly sought-after development of Whatley Hall, Archerswood, Clonee, Dublin 15. This property also qualifies for the Vacant Home Scheme, adding further appeal for prospective purchasers.\nWhatley Hall is a well-established residential development ideally positioned close to a wealth of local amenities including shops, cafés, leisure facilities and recreational amenities. Blanchardstown Shopping Centre is within easy reach, while commuters are exceptionally well catered for with easy access to the N3, M3 and M50 motorway networks, providing excellent links throughout Dublin and beyond.\nBright and spacious internal living accommodation extending to approximately c. 84 sq.m briefly comprises an entrance hallway, a generous open plan living/dining area with access to a private balcony, a fully fitted kitchen, two well-proportioned double bedrooms including a master bedroom with ensuite, together with a family bathroom.\nA standout feature of this fine property is the stunning private sunny balcony overlooking beautifully landscaped communal green areas, providing an ideal space to relax and unwind. The development also benefits from ample parking.\nNo.78  comes to the market with a B3 BER rating, gas fired central heating and double glazed windows. The annual management fee is approximately 2,500. This fantastic apartment is sure to appeal to first-time buyers, downsizers and investors alike.\nEarly viewing is strongly advised. Contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today for further information or to arrange a viewing.\nFeatures\n<ul>\n <li>BER B3 Rated\n• C. 84 sq.m\n• 2 Bed / 2 Bath apartment\n• Qualifies for Vacant Home Scheme\n• Private sunny balcony\n• Balcony overlooking landscaped green area\n• Gas fired central heating\n• Double glazed windows\n• Qualifies for a GREEN mortgage</li>\n <li> • Management fees c. 2,500 per annum</li>\n <li>• Quiet and well-established development\n• Popular and highly sought-after location\n• Close to shops and local amenities\n• Blanchardstown Shopping Centre within easy reach\n• Easy access to the N3, M3 & M50 motorway networks\n• NO-onward chain\n• Ideal for first-time buyers and downsizers\n• Early viewing strongly advised</li>\n</ul>"
      },
      {
